# AI Development Rules for <%= name.camelize %>

This document outlines the rules and guidelines for developing the <%= name.camelize %> Decidim module. These rules are designed to be used by an AI pair programmer to ensure consistency, quality, and adherence to the project's standards.

## 1. Core Principles

- **Modularity**: The module should be self-contained and have minimal dependencies on other modules.
- **Extensibility**: The module should be designed to be easily extended and customized.
- **Testability**: All code should be covered by automated tests.
- **Security**: The module must follow all Decidim security best practices.

## 2. Code Style

- Follow the official [Decidim Development Guide](https://docs.decidim.org/en/develop/).
- Adhere to the Ruby style guide and Rubocop rules defined in the project.

## 3. AI Collaboration Guidelines

- When generating code, the AI should always provide explanations for its choices.
- The AI should ask for clarification if the requirements are ambiguous.
- All generated code must include corresponding tests.
